  "notes": "{振|ふ}り{込|こ}む is a transitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}) used for bank transfers.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n- Pattern: [money]を [account]に {振|ふ}り{込|こ}む\n- Passive: {振|ふ}り{込|こ}まれる (commonly used for salary deposits)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {口座|こうざ}に{振|ふ}り{込|こ}む (transfer into an account)\n- {銀行|ぎんこう}に{振|ふ}り{込|こ}む (transfer to a bank)\n- {自動|じどう}{振|ふ}り{込|こ}み (automatic transfer)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {振|ふ}り{込|こ}み: noun form (bank transfer)\n- {振|ふ}り{込|こ}め{詐欺|さぎ}: wire transfer fraud (a common type of scam in Japan)\n- {送金|そうきん}: remittance (more general term)\n- {引|ひ}き{落|お}とし: automatic debit/withdrawal",
